  "notes": [
    "All benchmark policies use the same SIMD target arithmetic. Serial disables DSpark.",
    "Throughput is emitted tokens divided by full request time; decode and prefill rates are reported separately.",
    "Policies include the anchor: width 4 proposes 3 tokens, width 6 proposes 5 tokens.",
    "Every repeat matches serial and the corresponding pre-refactor fixture token-for-token.",
    "The 4096-token-budget runs in results.json and moe_results.json predate this ownership refactor and were not repeated here.",
    "Only the verify.py module docstring changed after GPU validation: MiniCPM adapter became MiniCPM verifier. Executable code is unchanged.",
    "Token SHA256 encodes compact JSON token arrays, using separators comma and colon.",
    "Complete token streams, per-round records and logs are retained in Downloads/MiniCPM-DSpark-ownership-validation."
  ]
